<section class="section" id="launch">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Launch event</span>
      <h2>Nuffield College, May 2023</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="launch">
      <figure class="launch__figure">
        <img class="launch__poster" src="{{ '/assets/img/book-launch-poster.jpg' | url }}"
             alt="Poster for the book launch event at Nuffield College, Oxford"
             width="620" height="877">
        <figcaption>Large Lecture Room, Nuffield College &middot; 16 May 2023</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p>The book was launched at Nuffield College, Oxford, three months after publication.
          It was chaired by <strong>Duncan Snidal</strong>, with comments from economists and
          political scientists whose work bears directly on the questions it takes up &mdash;
          the design of institutions, the measurement of opportunity, and the politics of
          international cooperation.</p>
        <p>The discussion ranged over the book&rsquo;s central claim &mdash; that the gravest
          threat to institutional performance comes from member states rather than from
          international bureaucrats &mdash; and over what follows from it for the reform of
          multilateral organisations at a moment when several are under strain.</p>
        <ul class="speakers">
          <li class="speaker"><span class="speaker__n">Duncan Snidal</span><span class="speaker__role">Chair</span><span class="speaker__a">University of Oxford</span></li>
          <li class="speaker"><span class="speaker__n">Joseph Stiglitz</span><span class="speaker__a">Columbia University</span></li>
          <li class="speaker"><span class="speaker__n">Raj Chetty</span><span class="speaker__a">Harvard University</span></li>
          <li class="speaker"><span class="speaker__n">Ranjit Lall</span><span class="speaker__a">University of Oxford</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

